course: dictionary
lesson: 5962
title: Mathematician
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mathematician is a person who studies maths deeply, or whose job is doing maths. They find new ideas, prove things and solve hard problems. The ending -ician is like musician or magician: it tells you someone is skilled at something.
explain: Clues in the sentence help. «Neptune was found in 1846 after mathematicians predicted where it must be from the way it tugged on Uranus.» Mathematicians worked out where Neptune had to be before anyone saw it. They used patterns and proof, not guessing.
explain: Being quick at sums is good, and someone who is very good at maths can be called a good mathematician. But a mathematician does more: they ask «what if?», explain why something is true, and prove it. «Many mathematicians call maths beautiful», because they love finding patterns.
fact: A mathematician is a person who studies maths deeply or whose job is doing maths.
fact: The plural of mathematician is mathematicians.
fact: Teachers may say «think like a mathematician»: notice patterns, ask «what if?», explain and prove.
fact: Famous mathematicians include Pythagoras, Hypatia, Ada Lovelace, Alan Turing, Katherine Johnson and Srinivasa Ramanujan.
fact: «The mathematician and astronomer Aryabhata, about 1,500 years ago, explained that the Earth spins.»
exercise: What is a mathematician? | *A person who studies maths deeply or whose job is doing maths | A teacher who only teaches music | A machine that counts coins | A person who sells fruit at a market
exercise: «Neptune was found in 1846 after mathematicians predicted where it must be.» What did the mathematicians do? | Named the planet Uranus | Sailed out to look for it | *Worked out where Neptune must be using patterns | Painted a picture of it
exercise: Which is the plural of mathematician? | mathematicion | *mathematicians | mathematicks | mathematicianses
test: Which word means a person who studies maths deeply? | Physicist | Biologist | Historian | *Mathematician
test: The ending -ician is like musician. What does it suggest? | Something that happened long ago | A place where something happens | *A person skilled at a subject or job | A very small thing
exam: Which sentence shows a mathematician at work? | «Priya ate her lunch quickly in the playground.» | «Priya used a pattern to prove the rule works for every number.» | *«Priya used a pattern to prove the rule works for every number, then explained why.» | «Priya bought a new pair of trainers.»
